iscovers a  murder in the green room they become  hostages backstage Patrick Stewart plays  the neo-nazi owner of the club who is  really good at covering his own tracks  at any crimes that happen there the late  Anton Yelchin delivers an amazing  performance as a musician who has to try  to step up and save his bandmates lives  what's surprising about green room is  that it takes a huge tonal turn that the  audience doesn't see coming even if they  know the plot while it is in a horror  film it does more for the genre than any  other movie this year writer-director  Jeremy Sonnier delivers a brilliantly  intense thriller that has some real  cringe-worthy violent scenes it does  have some gory moments much like the saw  or hostile series however green room has  much more well-rounded characters and a  cohesive plot coming seventh on our list  Ryan Gosling and Russell Crowe star as  the nice guys a duo who are either the  world's best or worse detectives we're  leaning towards the latter this comedic  trip through 1970s la works mostly  because of the undeniable presents from  and the chemistry between its two stars  you're in the pool yeah why I had to  question the mermaids what were you  doing while I was working writer  director Shane Black create some  extraordinary circumstances for them the  unlikely pair is forced to work together  to solve a case where nothing is quite  what it seems to be its lethal weapon  with a whole lot more sleeves in  slapstick and it totally worked for us  rough Deadpool owns the six spot on this  list for a number of reasons it  revolutionized the stale comic book  genre and also made us completely forget  about this travesty  Wade Wilson is a medical experiment gone  wrong and a comic book movie experiment  done right it broke all the comic book  movie cliches to share the story of an  explicit foul mouth antihero it's an  action-packed visual stunner laugh out  loud funny and a hell of a good time oh  I'm touching myself tonight number five  is kubo and the two strings in an age  where cg effects can render the visually  impossible into a mundane reality the  craftsmanship and patience that a  stop-motion film like kubo requires is  absolutely mind-blowing you never want  to take your eyes away from the screen  here and as kubo himself says in the  film if he must blink do it now but  forget about the outstanding technical  achievement that is kubo kubo and the  two strings made it onto our list of  best films of the year because of its  wonderful heartfelt story which is at  once a grand fable and also a deeply  personal film about family and  relationships kubo is the best type of  family film a grand adventure a rousing  tale all ring from a place of emotional  truth at number 4 is Captain America  Civil War comic book fans have seen  heroes fighting other heroes time and  time again it's only natural we'd see  the same happen on the big screen in the  Marvel Cinematic Universe after seeing  the Avengers team up to fight incredible  odds there now fighting for screen time  as the foundation of the team begins to  crumble Civil War re-examined the way  the Marvel heroes can operate instead of  following the same formula that worked a  dozen times Marvel Studios tried  something different even with the movie  crammed full of superheroes they managed  to introduce some more not that I'm not  ah yeah I'm not number three is 10  Cloverfield Lane the original 2008  Cloverfield was a found-footage monster  movie the story followed six characters  making their way across New York City 10  Cloverfield Lane takes a completely  different approach with only three cast  members and a third person POV the  majority of the movie happens in the  confines of a bomb shelter the tension  was only amped up by having John Goodman  thrusting his hips while dancing in  front of a jukebox easter shower the  suit is an awkward moments at the dinner  table at a time where movie trailers act  as a concise summary of the entire movie  10 Cloverfield Lane managed to contain  plenty of suspense and twists to catch  the audience's off guard the less you  know about the plot and the constrictive  environment makes this a movie that will  keep you on the edge of your seat just  make sure you're not seated next to  someone that's ready to smash a bottle  over your head number two is rogue one a  movie set in the Star Wars universe  seems like a no-brainer when the movie  focuses on a cast of brand new  characters it's a whole new ballgame  apart from moving away from the familiar  heroes we've grown to love the film  shifts the tone we might expect by  showing more realistic aspects of an  intergalactic war we've seen nameless  rebel trooper shot down and paid little  attention to it our cast here is on a  mission against massive odds and doesn't  have the luxury of giant wiki's or fancy  lightsabers to save their butts there's  a nice mix of old and new Star Wars  elements we have to see new planets  characters and ships set within a  familiar time period the filmmakers have  shown that there are other areas the  Star Wars mythos that can be explored  outside the saga movies the tone is a  little darker than you might expect but  there is also plenty of humor and hope  rebellions of built home hope and coming  in at number one arrival this wasn't  even debated the film was amazing and  this was the best-looking seen in any  film this year  Amy Adams is mixture of fear and  interest when she first sets eyes on the  aliens was exactly how we would have  felt in the same situation the only  difference is we would have seen our  hazmat suits apart from amazing acting  and beautiful visuals this film has an  effect on the way you see the world  after watching it as the story  progresses it changes our understanding  of the concepts of time language and  handshakes that's a proper introduction  and those are top movies of 2016 for  more movie nerdiness plus TV and comics  stick with game